<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Nunito:wght@400;600;700;800&display=swap');
  body{font-family:'Nunito','ABC Arizona Sans',Calibri,sans-serif;color:#1A1A1A;font-size:11pt;margin:0}
  .wrap{padding:26px 34px 30px}
  h1{font-family:'Nunito',Georgia,serif;color:#2f6df0;font-size:24pt;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 4px}
  h2{font-family:'Nunito',Georgia,serif;color:#2f6df0;font-size:15pt;font-weight:800;margin:18px 0 5px}
  p{margin:3px 0}.sub{color:#1A1A1A;font-size:11pt}.lbl{font-weight:800;color:#2f6df0;margin-top:8px}.bul{margin-left:20px}.ind{margin-left:14px}
 </style></head><body><div class="wrap"><h1>Advice Request – David &amp; Lisa Hartmann</h1><p class="sub">Adviser: Hayden Wilson</p><p class="sub">(ACCUMULATOR SOA · Couple · Existing client)</p><div style="height:7px"></div><p>Hi Team,</p><p>David &amp; Lisa are existing clients. They want to retain their SMSF and establish an investment portfolio in the SMSF name, cancel personal insurances, consolidate the car loan into the home loan, and switch the investment property loan to interest only.</p><div style="height:7px"></div><div style="height:7px"></div><h2>Risk Profile</h2><div style="height:7px"></div><h2>Scope of Advice</h2><p>1 · Debt Management</p><p>2 · Investment Property</p><p>3 · Investment Bond</p><p>4 · Investment Plan</p><p>5 · Personal Superannuation</p><p>6 · Superannuation Contributions</p><p>7 · Personal Protection</p><p>8 · Cashflow Management &amp; Budgeting</p><div style="height:7px"></div><h2>1 · Debt Management Advice</h2><p class="lbl">Strategy Recommendations</p><p class="bul">• Both: We recommend consolidating your existing car loan into your home loan.</p><p class="bul">• Both: We recommend you switch your investment property loan(s) from principal &amp; interest to interest only to improve cashflow and maintain tax-deductible debt.</p><div style="height:7px"></div><h2>5 · Personal Superannuation Advice</h2><p class="lbl">Strategy Recommendations</p><p class="bul">• Both: We recommend you retain your existing SMSF.</p><div style="height:7px"></div><h2>Advice Fees</h2></div></body></html>